      "quality": "poor",
      "qualityReason": "location_description"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The lake covers 48.6 acres and reaches a maximum depth of 20 feet, making it one of the shallower lakes in Snohomish County.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        8
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://snohomishcountywa.gov/5396/Sunday",
      "category": "nature",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Sunday Lake’s watershed spans 851.3 acres, mostly undeveloped, and drains into the lake from the surrounding plateau.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        9
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://snohomishcountywa.gov/5396/Sunday",
      "category": "nature",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Boating on Sunday Lake is restricted to non‑gasoline motors, and a walk‑in boat launch is available on the north side.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        10,
        11
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://snohomishcountywa.gov/5396/Sunday",
      "category": "other",
      "quality": "poor",
      "qualityReason": "other"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "The 2019 Algae Control Plan, created with community input, aims to cut phosphorus pollution—the main cause of toxic algae blooms.",
